  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.4.0 - compatible with 1.3 in both directions; all new behavior is opt-in.\n\nNew:\n- Server push: Server.SendAsync(clientId, message), BroadcastAsync(message), ConnectedClients.\n- Client ids on server-side events and in the new RequestContext.\n- Request cancellation: a timed-out or cancelled SendAndWaitAsync stops the handler on a 1.4 server (OnRequest overload with RequestContext.CancellationToken).\n- MaxConcurrentRequests (default 1, as before) runs a client's requests in parallel.\n- KeepAlive for TCP and CurrentUserOnly for named pipes.\n\nFixed:\n- PipeServer busy-looped while idle, and could drop clients during connection bursts on Linux and macOS.\n- Late replies to timed-out requests no longer show up as MessageReceived events.\n- A throwing ClientConnected subscriber no longer stops a TcpServer accepting clients.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\nSamples: https://github.com/hamedafzali/HRpc/blob/main/docs/SAMPLES.md",
